{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9113f6895bb3c1522a19b0a14958f15cd80e1e2e30ceb732f73c30274b98611a","digest":{"component_or_area":"outbound type mapping and inbound recovery","key_entities":["config.effective_type_map","config.assert_type_decisions_complete","config.effective_excluded_sync_types","config.jira_to_local_type","LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA","EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES","mapping_config.SKIP","rebar-type:","outbound_labels._REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX","outbound_labels._desired_type_annotation","outbound_labels._diff_type_annotation_labels","inbound_fields.recover_type_label","inbound_fields._LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB","outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields","outbound_differ.compute_outbound_mutations","outbound_mutation_builders._compute_outbound_create_mutation","TicketType","OutboundMapper"],"problem_keywords":["type mapping","config-driven","type-granular skip","round-trip safety","rebar annotation","type resolution","fail-closed"],"propositions":["Config-driven type mapping must resolve local ticket types to Jira types per-project, with support for remapping and per-project SKIP exclusions, symmetrically with status mapping.","Type resolution must fail closed before the mutation loop begins, raising MappingConfigError if any syncable type lacks a decision (mapped target or SKIP).","The rebar-type: annotation label must be stamped symmetrically with rebar-status: when type mapping is lossy (collapsing local types to one Jira type), using a reverse Jira-to-local map for round-trip detection.","Type map and effective excluded set (builtin EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES union per-project SKIP entries) must be threaded through all three OutboundMapper implementations and both field mappers, with signature consistency.","The rebar-type: prefix must be added to internal label exclusion tuples in outbound_labels, inbound_collection_diffs, differ, inbound_translate to prevent it syncing as a user tag or spurious mutation.","Inbound recovery via recover_type_label must restore the original local type from the rebar-type: label, reverse-map-free, with LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB derived from TicketType union args."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787724527803142001,"uuid":"8aa5e18d-f8b5-4a4a-9ce1-9a3fa975886f"}